And even though one such became a valiant chieftain, brave, a taker of captives, indeed he sold and yielded himself to slavery; he became someone&#8217;s digging stick and tump line; he yielded to the digging stick and tump line. So it was said: &#8220;Thus was his day sign; thus was his life. On such a day was he born; thus was his birthright.&#8221;

